   "last_comment": "In my understanding with 2 weeks of reading this stuff, yes. CILogon is not FedRamp and therefore trusting its authentication brings it into the boundary. So we may not be able to use it for authenticating into CUI clusters.",
   "summary": "knikolla's tentative answer is yes: CILogon is not FedRAMP, so trusting it pulls it into the boundary and it may not be usable for logging in to CUI clusters. If that holds it cuts against the CILogon federation in the #282 IdP decision; nobody has responded yet.",
   "summary_reviewed": "2026-09-21"
